        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "81fafa11-f720-5b96-9545-343f0200fcbf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alison Moyet, Mike Muir, Michael Seiff\n- Bands: Suicidal Tendencies, Los Cycos, Infectious Grooves\n- Songs and Albums: When I Was Your Girl, The Minutes, Welcome to Venice\n- Organizations: Suicidal Records\n- Places: Venice, California\n\nFacts:\n- Alison Moyet, born Geneviève Alison Jane Moyet on 18 June 1961, is an English singer, songwriter, and performer known for her bluesy contralto voice.\n- Mike Muir, born Michael Allen Muir on March 14, 1963, is the lead vocalist of the Venice, California bands Suicidal Tendencies, Los Cycos, and Infectious Grooves.\n- Welcome to Venice was produced by Mike Muir.\n- Welcome to Venice featured cover art by Michael Seiff, who later created art for the other three original Suicidal Records releases.\n- When I Was Your Girl is a song by Alison Moyet.\n- When I Was Your Girl was released as the first single from Alison Moyet's eighth studio album, The Minutes.\n- The Minutes debuted at number five on the UK Albums Chart on 12 May 2013.",
